This project contains only code of our own (MIT, see LICENSE).

At runtime it uses:
  - GLib and Gio (LGPL-2.1+), through GObject Introspection - for the main
    loop and the subscription to UPower
  - gsettings from glib2.0-bin (LGPL-2.1+), to read and set
    org.gnome.desktop.interface gtk-theme and icon-theme
  - UPower (GPL-2.0+), only as a clock: one signal is subscribed to, nothing
    is called and nothing is changed

It reads, without changing them:
  - /sys/class/power_supply/battery/{status,current_now,voltage_now,capacity}
  - the battery icons of the Adwaita icon theme (CC-BY-SA 3.0 / LGPL-3), as
    the source for its own copies

It creates, under ~/.local/share/icons and ~/.themes:
  - three GTK 3 themes consisting of an @import line onto the user's own
    theme plus one colour rule
  - an icon theme `furios-battery` that inherits the user's own and replaces
    eight battery icons with versions whose filling is a path of its own

The user's own theme - adw-gtk3 (MIT) on this phone - and the Adwaita icons
are neither copied wholesale, nor changed, nor relicensed; `battctl restore`
removes everything that was generated.

No part of FuriOS is patched or replaced.
